.TH SESSLINT-COMPLETION 1 "" "SessLint 0.4.1" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-completion \- [read\-only] Print shell completion script.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint completion {bash,zsh,fish,powershell}
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Print a shell completion script generated from the live parser.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B {bash,zsh,fish,powershell}
Shell dialect (bash, zsh, fish, powershell)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
a clean session exits 0
(also verification passed / dry-run plan generated)
.TP
.B 1
a session with findings exits 1
(also verification failed / repair refused)
.TP
.B 2
an internal tool error exits 2
(also usage error / invalid flags / I/O failure)
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

